Hint: 

Timestamps are in Unix time which can be looked up online,
 or gotten from converting seconds after January 1, 1970 UTC (we are 5 hours behind UTC)

Just give them one of the early fields if need more hints


Key:
Note times done with [DateTimeOffset]::FromUnixTimeSeconds(1792780800).ToLocalTime() (powershell command),
but can be grabbed anywhere from online

DNS — 1:40 PM Dallas time: 172.16.0.15 queries the DNS server for the company's domain.
SSL — 1:41:40 PM Dallas time: The same origin host connects to the HTTPS server.
HTTP — 6:40 PM Dallas time: 172.16.0.16 sends a successful HTTP GET request to the same domain.

Attack is the HTTP log to DuckCompany.archived.oldwebsite.com

1792780800.0 for the dns log (that day at like pretty early)
1792780900.0 for ssl log (since dns and ssl are non-malicious since not downgrade)
1792798800.0 for the http log (recent)

